> In my previous roles, I have adopted a supportive and collaborative approach to managing early-career researchers. I believe in fostering an environment where they feel valued and empowered to contribute their ideas. 
> 
> 1. **Mentorship and Guidance**: I prioritize regular one-on-one meetings to discuss their projects, provide feedback, and offer career advice. This open line of communication helps them feel supported and encourages their professional growth.
> 
> 2. **Encouraging Independence**: While I provide guidance, I also encourage them to take ownership of their work. I set clear expectations and allow them to explore their research questions independently, which boosts their confidence and critical thinking skills.
> 
